%description:

Tcp.mtuProbing:search-probe-lost -- a lost probe lowers the top of the search: the next probe is smaller.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "RFC 4821 - Packetization Layer Path MTU Discovery. By parameter
(mtuProbing = 2 ...): a search between baseMss and the MSS of the peer, with one probe segment
from queued data ... The route MTU bounds the search".

The class search-probe-lost: TcpConnection::sendSegment() finds the retransmission of the data
of a probe, and mtuProbeFailed() sets the top of the search below the size of the probe. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part.
This test separates "search" from "off", which sends no probe.

Host under test: host1; host1 sends 1000000 bytes at 0.2 s, and the tap drops the first frame
of host1 above 1100 bytes, the first probe. Observation: level 1, the next frame of host1 above
1100 bytes is smaller than the lost probe.

%# parameter: Tcp.mtuProbing
%# class: search-probe-lost
%# value: 2
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mtuProbing
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMtuProbingSearchProbeLost")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 1100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the first frame of host1 above 1100 bytes, the first probe"))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 1100B")
             .capture("probe", "ipv4.totalLengthField")
             .describe("the first probe")
             .within(1.0))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 1100B")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField < {probe}")
             .describe("the next probe")
             .within(1.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMtuProbingSearchProbeLost compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mtuProbing = 2    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
sim-time-limit = 3s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMtuProbingSearchProbeLost: PASS
